+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The network LOOKS scribbled, not engineered — every bundle draws as a straight node-center-to-center band that crosses sibling pipes, runs through node sprites, and terminates buried under the puck, so the bird's-eye picture reads as random chalk lines instead of a designed network.
+
+**Approach:** Make the DRAWN wire path a presentation-only, deterministic polyline that (1) detours around crossings/node sprites/map edges, (2) attaches at router puck rim anchors allocated evenly around the puck (the clean 4-pipe ✕/＋ read), (3) renders parallel-pipe bundles as ONE ribbon that fans open at each end to the member anchors, and (4) degrades to straight when a detour would be longer/uglier than the crossing. Cost stays on the LOGICAL straight A→B geometry (`pipe_span × cost_per_tile`) — the detour never touches gameplay. **SHIPPED VERDICT (lavish gate 2026-08-19, verbatim): "Ship pure straight (routing OFF, anchors OFF) — Story 7.5 becomes routing-only infrastructure."** The mechanism ships complete + tested + cost-immune; the shipped render keeps both flags off, so T2 goldens are byte-identical (NO re-bless).
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Path computation lives in a NEW pure view module `app/render/wire_path.odin` (ODN-1: reads topology/bundles/catalogs only, never writes sim state; deterministic from topology + view + world bounds — same map → same paths, no RNG, seed-independent).
+- Cost immunity: `draw_cost(span, tier, cat)` keeps using the LOGICAL integer Euclidean span (node centers), never the drawn path. Pinned by a test: identical costs for identical topology regardless of routing, and T1 state-hash + replay byte-identical `[E10]`.
+- All drawn-path consumers follow the SAME path: the band + lane stripes + congestion halo (draw_bundles), packet riders (draw_packets — riders ride the ribbon, arc-length parameterized, lateral lane offset preserved), the selection halo, the crisis bottleneck outline, and the committed-bundle assist glow.
+- Anchor allocation: at a router, n incident pipes get n anchors evenly spread around the puck, aligned to the incident directions (deterministic, snapped to the pinned CIRCLE16 table — no transcendentals in the rasterized path, §10.4). Terminal endpoints attach at the building footprint edge toward the router (the doorstep language; 7.1 queued packets stay at the doorstep).
+- Bundles with count>1 draw ONE pooled ribbon mid-span (7.1 band_width unchanged) that fans open at each end into the member pipes' anchors (thin member-width stubs anchor→fan apex).
+- Degradation: named thresholds `WIRE_DETOUR_MAX_LEN_RATIO` + `WIRE_DETOUR_MAX_BENDS` (render-side constants, the PULSE16/ROUTER_TIER_SCALE precedent — never catalog-poisoned). When a detour exceeds the ratio or still crosses after the bend cap → STRAIGHT. Terminal stubs (short building drops) stay straight unless they clip a node sprite.
+- Obstacles: OTHER bundles' straight logical segments (order-free, pure function of topology), node/terminal sprite footprints (excluding the path's own endpoint nodes), and the world-edge margin.
+- Graceful degradation to the pre-7.5 render is one View flag (`route_wires`, default true): the gate's "straight" side and any emergency fallback share it.
+
+**Ask First:** none — the aesthetic verdict (curve style, clearance feel, fan look) is the USER's at the mandatory lavish gate; the gate iterates until an explicit approve, and the approved style is what ships.
+
+**Never:** No gameplay changes (FORGE #2 crossings never punished), no core/sim/catalog changes, no new node/terminal art, no map/terrain changes (terrain-aware routing = named follow-up, FLAG not build), no LOG_VERSION bump, no serialization change, no RNG anywhere in the path, no transcendentals in the rasterized path.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| HAPPY_PATH | sparse map, bundle A→B clear | straight band A→B (pre-7.5 pixels) | n/a |
+| CROSSING | A→B crosses bundle C→D | path bends to slide alongside C→D at clearance | bend cap + ratio → straight if absurd |
+| CLIPPING | A→B passes through a third node's sprite | path bends around the sprite footprint | same |
+| MAP EDGE | A→B would run within edge margin | path inset from the edge | same |
+| 4 pipes at a router | router with 4 incident pipes | 4 anchors at 90° (✕/＋ read), bands emerge from the rim | n≥1; 1 pipe = single anchor |
+| BUNDLE FAN | 2 parallel pipes R1↔R2 | one ribbon mid-span, 2 member stubs at each end | count=1 → no fan |
+| TERMINAL STUB | short building drop crossing a pipe | stays straight (crossing is the right look) | unless sprite clip |
+| DEGRADED | dense core, every detour worse | straight fallback (never zigzag into absurdity) | deterministic |
+| EMPTY | no bundles | no path work, zero pixels | n/a |
