+## Design Notes
+
+The path is a fixed-size polyline (stack array, no frame-arena churn beyond one temp slice per frame in draw_world). Determinism comes from iterating bundles in slot order and treating other bundles' STRAIGHT logical segments as obstacles — a pure function of topology, so path order is irrelevant (order-free by construction). Riders sample via arc length (`wire_path_point`) so a packet that rides a detoured ribbon stays ON the ribbon at the same logical progress. All thresholds are named render constants; tuning them at the gate is a one-line change, never a catalog edit (catalog edits are golden-poisoned — the field-notes trap).
